> Window Management

Window management is done primarily through your keyboard, with mouse options available.

Within mango, windows automatically lay themselves out depending on your configured layout.
you can tweak the layout at any time using *SUPER+SHIFT+W*.

the different layouts are covered in 105 - layouts.

### General

[^SUPER+Q]: close window
quits the active window, like pressing X on a desktop.

[^SUPER+T]: float/unfloat window
floated windows appear above tiled applications and do not tile.

[^SUPER+F]: toggle fullscreen
puts the application in front of tiled and floating windows but behind overlay.

[^SUPER+ALT+F]: toggle fake fullscreen
tells the app it's fullscreen but keeps it tiled. useful to hide top bars and decoration.

[^SUPER+SHIFT+P]: toggle overlay mode
shows over everything regardless of tiled, floating or fullscreen state.

[^SUPER+P]: pin window (global)
makes the window stay on screen regardless of workspace/tag. toggle to unpin.

[^SUPER+A]: special layout toggle
dwindle: maximizes focused window (windowed, covers all others)
scroller: changes scroller ratio for focused window
grid layouts: toggles gaps
deck and master/stack (tile): swaps focused window with master

[^ALT+TAB]: toggle and tab through overview
shows all windows on current monitor. hold alt and press tab to cycle.
release alt to open the selected window's workspace.
left click to open, right click to close.

[^SUPER+SHIFT+A]: cycle through common layouts
configured in layouts.conf via circle_layout. default cycle:
dwindle -> scroller -> vertical scroller -> center tile -> tile

### Workspace-related

[^SUPER+1-9]: switch to workspace

[^SUPER+SHIFT+1-9]: move focused window to workspace

[^SUPER+ALT+1-9]: toggle workspace visibility
mango lets you view multiple tags at once. toggles visibility of a workspace.

### Scratchpad

[^SUPER+CTRL+C]: move window to scratchpad
minimizes the focused window to the monitor's scratchpad. multiple windows can be stored.

[^SUPER+ALT+C]: move window out of scratchpad
brings last focused scratchpad window back out.

[^SUPER+C]: open/close scratchpad
cycles through windows in the current monitor's scratchpad.

[^SUPER+ALT+SPACE]: toggle terminal scratchpad
special scratchpad for a ghostty terminal. if no terminal exists, spawns one.
if one exists but isn't in scratchpad, pulls it in.
SNAPS-OS pre-loads one ghostty instance to the main monitor's terminal scratchpad.

### Arrow Keys

[^SUPER+ARROWS]: move focus between windows

[^SUPER+SHIFT+LEFT/RIGHT]: focus previous/next (stack-based layouts)

[^SUPER+SHIFT+UP/DOWN]: exchange stack clients (prev/next in tile layouts)

[^SUPER+ALT+ARROWS]: resize window

### Mouse Binds

[^SUPER+LEFTCLICK-DRAG]: drag and drop window
window is temporarily floating while dragged; shows where it will tile.

[^SUPER+RIGHTCLICK-DRAG]: resize window
for tiled windows, constrained by adjacent windows.

[^SUPER+MIDDLECLICK]: maximize window
keeps tiled but uses full window area (top bar still visible).
